  <document-link format="APPLICATION/VND.OPENXMLFORMATS-OFFICEDOCUMENT.WORDPROCESSINGML.DOCUMENT" url="https://iatipublisher-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/document-link/92/YFP%20Narrative%20Report%20July-%20December1711973440.docx">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY IMPACT OF YFP I (Sept. 2022), II (Jan. 2023), and III (Sept. 2023)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY IMPACT OF YFP I (Sept. 2022), II (Jan. 2023), and III (Sept. 2023)

How many youths have participated in the program? 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 1: 130 applications received, 20 youth were pre-selected, 16 youth participated and completed the training program. 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 2: 185 applications received, 36 youth were pre-selected, 25 youth were onboarded and received soft skills training.
&#x25CF;	Both times drop- out levels were high. Various reasons; school, family members being sick, rather focus on entrepreneurship. See learning of this below. 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 3: 340 applications received, 50 youth were selected for the cohort (10 directly for Warc in Tumu via Plan International), + and 4 additional youth were selected to accommodate for dropouts

How much (in percentage) have been connected with companies through our program?
&#x25CF;	Cohort 1: 16 (100%) gained traineeships 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 2: 19 (76%) gained traineeships 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 3: 30 (60%) gained employment- still ongoing till the end of Feb 2024 

Impact- How many youths have received a job offer through the program?
&#x25CF;	Cohort 1: 10 (62.5%) of 16 youth are still employed after 1 year from the start of their contract. 
&#x25CF;	Cohort 2: 12 (48%) are still in employment after placement/Traineeship (after 1 year) 
&#x25CF;	Cohort: 30 (60%) gained employment</narrative>
   </description>
